<title>USA: Consumers 67 MW nuke seen back up mid-week.</title>
<headline>Consumers 67 MW nuke seen back up mid-week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Consumers Power Co's 67 megawatt Big Rock Point nuclear power plant will likely resume power in the middle of this week after being shut for repairs, a company spokesman said Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;We expect it to return to service in the middle of the week,&quot; spokesman Tim Petrosky said.</p>
<p>The unit, in Charlevoix, Mich., was shut over the weekend due to an unstable main generator field current.</p>
<p>Consumers Power is a subsidiary of CMS Energy Corp.</p>
<p>--New York Power Desk +1 212 859 1627</p>
</text>
